Chapter: RPSWasm
  cites Games chapter RPS
  cites Games chapter Rng
  cites Foreword chapter List

 The browser interface for Rock Paper Scissors, on the handle contract in
 games-backlog.md GAME-11. Two count triples and three tallies are past an
 i32, so the page holds the state's address.

 `rps-do-round` writes both count lists with `list-set-at`, which mutates in
 place, so `rps-wasm-round` copies first.

 Moves are 0 rock, 1 paper, 2 scissors.

 We say:

Section: Copying

  rps-copy-counts : List Integer -> List Integer
  rps-copy-counts (src) =
    list-push (list-push (list-push [] (list-at src 0)) (list-at src 1)) (list-at src 2)

  rps-copy-state : RPSState -> RPSState
  rps-copy-state (s) =
    RPSState {
      p1-counts = rps-copy-counts (s.p1-counts),
      p2-counts = rps-copy-counts (s.p2-counts),
      p1-wins   = s.p1-wins,
      p2-wins   = s.p2-wins,
      ties      = s.ties,
      rng       = s.rng
    }

Section: The Browser Interface

  rps-wasm-new : Integer -> RPSState
  rps-wasm-new (seed) = rps-init seed

  rps-wasm-round : RPSState -> RPSState
  rps-wasm-round (s) = rps-do-round (rps-copy-state s)

  rps-wasm-p1-count : RPSState, Integer -> Integer
  rps-wasm-p1-count (s) (m) =
    if m < 0 then (-1)
    else if m >= 3 then (-1)
    else list-at (s.p1-counts) m

  rps-wasm-p2-count : RPSState, Integer -> Integer
  rps-wasm-p2-count (s) (m) =
    if m < 0 then (-1)
    else if m >= 3 then (-1)
    else list-at (s.p2-counts) m

  rps-wasm-p1-wins : RPSState -> Integer
  rps-wasm-p1-wins (s) = s.p1-wins

  rps-wasm-p2-wins : RPSState -> Integer
  rps-wasm-p2-wins (s) = s.p2-wins

  rps-wasm-ties : RPSState -> Integer
  rps-wasm-ties (s) = s.ties

Section: The Rules, Exposed for Grading

  rps-wasm-beats : Integer -> Integer
  rps-wasm-beats (m) = rps-beats m

  rps-wasm-outcome : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  rps-wasm-outcome (m1) (m2) = rps-outcome m1 m2

 The AI's choice is exposed with the opponent's counts and a seed, which is
 what the engine itself passes it. The seed is the whole Rng: a grader
 sweeping seeds over one fixed count triple sees the distribution of
 choices, and the fuzz branch is a minority of it.

  rps-wasm-choice : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  rps-wasm-choice (c0) (c1) (c2) (seed) =
    let counts = list-push (list-push (list-push [] c0) c1) c2
    in rps-weighted-move counts (rng-new seed)

Section: The Whole Series

  rps-wasm-run : Integer, Integer -> RPSResult
  rps-wasm-run (seed) (rounds) = run-rps-series seed rounds

  rps-wasm-res-p1 : RPSResult -> Integer
  rps-wasm-res-p1 (r) = r.p1-wins

  rps-wasm-res-p2 : RPSResult -> Integer
  rps-wasm-res-p2 (r) = r.p2-wins

  rps-wasm-res-ties : RPSResult -> Integer
  rps-wasm-res-ties (r) = r.ties

